## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a tiny 3-valued solver: propagation, clash detection, and controlled backtracking while preserving non-boolean placeholders.

## Key Concepts
- 3-valued logic propagation
- Forward-checking and fixpoint computation
- Backtracking with Unknowns to preserve flexibility

## Code Example
```javascript
function propagate(vars, constraints) {
  // vars: {S1: T|F|U, S2: T|F|U, S3: T|F|U}
  // constraints: list of functions returning {changed, ok}
  // Minimal sketch for illustration
  let changed = true;
  while (changed) {
    changed = false;
    for (const c of constraints) {
      const res = c(vars);
      if (res.changed) changed = true;
      if (!res.ok) return {ok: false};
    }
  }
  return {ok: true, vars};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This probes designing a 3-valued constraint propagator with a nontrivial rule and a forced Unknown branching, mirroring how production systems reason about partial information.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic (H>U> N) and definition of implication as ¬A ∨ B
- Constraint propagation and fixpoint computation
- Backtracking on U choices to avoid definite F outcomes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal 3-valued logic helpers
const order = {H:2, U:1, N:0};
function not(v){ return v==='H'?'N': v==='N'?'H':'U'; }
function and(a,b){ return order[a] <= order[b] ? a : b; }
function or(a,b){ return order[a] >= order[b] ? a : b; }
function implies(a,b){ return or(not(a), b); }
```

